{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "actions": {
    "external": [
      {
        "action": "app.quit",
        "chord": "Ctrl+Q",
        "consumer": "semu-input-supervisor",
        "semantics": "immediate process-group termination"
      }
    ]
  },
  "compiler": {
    "bindings": {
      "profile_name": {
        "source": "emulator.name"
      },
      "input_driver": {
        "source": "platform.retroarch.input_driver"
      },
      "audio_driver": {
        "source": "platform.retroarch.audio_driver"
      },
      "content_root": {
        "source": "runtime.content_root"
      },
      "hotkey_enable_hotkey_btn": {
        "source": "input.retroarch_hotkeys.enable_hotkey_btn"
      },
      "hotkey_save_state_btn": {
        "source": "input.retroarch_hotkeys.save_state_btn"
      },
      "hotkey_load_state_btn": {
        "source": "input.retroarch_hotkeys.load_state_btn"
      },
      "hotkey_menu_toggle_btn": {
        "source": "input.retroarch_hotkeys.menu_toggle_btn"
      },
      "hotkey_toggle_fast_forward_btn": {
        "source": "input.retroarch_hotkeys.toggle_fast_forward_btn"
      },
      "hotkey_rewind_btn": {
        "source": "input.retroarch_hotkeys.rewind_btn"
      },
      "hotkey_screenshot_btn": {
        "source": "input.retroarch_hotkeys.screenshot_btn"
      },
      "video_driver": {
        "source": "platform.retroarch.video_driver"
      },
      "bios_directory": {
        "source": "runtime.bios_directory"
      },
      "joypad_driver": {
        "source": "platform.retroarch.joypad_driver"
      }
    },
    "line_groups": {
      "keyboard_hotkey_defaults": {
        "kind": "collisions",
        "rows": "keyboard_defaults.hotkeys",
        "format": "${setting} = \"nul\"",
        "chord_encoding_of": "keymap_hotkeys",
        "except_rows": "hotkeys.keymap",
        "always": [
          "input_shader_toggle",
          "input_shader_next",
          "input_shader_prev"
        ]
      },
      "keyboard_player_defaults": {
        "kind": "collisions",
        "rows": "keyboard_defaults.player1",
        "format": "${setting} = \"nul\"",
        "chord_encoding_of": "keymap_hotkeys",
        "platforms": [
          "linux"
        ]
      },
      "keymap_hotkeys": {
        "rows": "hotkeys.keymap",
        "format": "${setting} = \"${chord}\"",
        "formats": {
          "linux": "${setting} = \"nul\""
        },
        "chord_encoding": {
          "mode": "joined",
          "ignore_modifiers": true,
          "key_case": "lower",
          "keys": {
            "+": "add",
            "-": "subtract",
            "Esc": "escape"
          }
        },
        "prefix": [
          "input_quit_gamepad_combo = \"0\""
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "doc": {
    "purpose": "RetroArch profile content (retroarch.cfg, golden line order) as data, substituted by RetroArchEmitter. The visual block emits fullscreen raw output with native shaders and smoothing disabled; session-specific driver and scaling pins are runtime upserts owned by RetroArchRendering.",
    "variables": "${profile_name} contract name; ${input_driver}/${audio_driver} resolved by the emulator class (lines drop when empty); ${content_root} the shared runtime content root.",
    "keyboard": "RetroArch polls its keymap once a frame (XQueryKeymap), so it can miss a short Steam tap and would act a second time beside the supervisor. On Linux targets the supervisor reads every keyboard chord (evdev, and the X raw-key adapter in Game Mode) and drives RetroArch over the command port, so the keymap rows Semu compiles are \"nul\" there (formats.linux) and so is every player-1 default whose key a Semu chord uses (keyboard_player_defaults). macOS has no keyboard source in its supervisor and keeps the keymap and the player keys. On every target the hotkey defaults that collide with a Semu chord are cleared, plus RetroArch's own shader hotkeys because Semu's renderer owns shaders (keyboard_hotkey_defaults). A collision is a default whose key equals a chord's key as keymap_hotkeys encodes it, modifiers ignored, as RetroArch ignores them.",
    "screen_swap": "Every DS and 3DS core swaps its screens on a pad button, which moves the picture into the wrong bezel hole and the taps to the wrong screen, and Semu cannot see a swapped frame (its size is unchanged). Each core remap file (RetroArch loads <input_remapping_directory>/<library_name>/<library_name>.rmp, -1 unmapped) takes that button away: melonDS R2 (input.cpp:59), Azahar and Citra L3 (also Citra's HOME), DeSmuME R3 (Quick Screen Switch, libretro.cpp:2011). The folder names are each core's retro_get_system_info library_name.",
    "pointer": "Taps reach the core as RETRO_DEVICE_POINTER from the window pointer RetroArch reads, so RetroArch must never grab the mouse (a grab turns it into warped deltas): video_windowed_fullscreen and input_auto_mouse_grab are pinned to their desktop defaults (config.def.h:252, 1610). auto_remaps_enable and input_remap_sort_by_controller_enable are pinned too, so the core remap files below load from where Semu writes them.",
    "players": "One input_playerN_joypad_index per player of the system (for_each players): the pad the player holds, by its place in the launch's roster (slot order, which is RetroArch's own order for Steam's virtual pads); a player without a pad gets an index no present pad has, so RetroArch's default (player N reads pad N-1) never hands one pad to two players. Without a roster (macOS) only player 1 is written, on pad 0, as before."
  },
  "keyboard_defaults": {
    "source": "RetroArch 69a4f0ea1e8aaf442ae4858f2e7f2b31a1776576 config.def.keybinds.h retro_keybinds_1, the #else (desktop, not Lakka) block at lines 1345-2015, every bind with a key; setting names from configuration.c input_config_bind_map (DECLARE_BIND/DECLARE_META_BIND, lines 299-414) and key names from input/input_keymaps.c input_config_key_map (lines 84-160). Vendored as data so a new Semu chord that takes one of these keys is cleared by the collision groups, never silently shared.",
    "player1": [
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_b",
        "key": "z"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_y",
        "key": "a"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_select",
        "key": "rshift"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_start",
        "key": "enter"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_up",
        "key": "up"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_down",
        "key": "down"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_left",
        "key": "left"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_right",
        "key": "right"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_a",
        "key": "x"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_x",
        "key": "s"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_l",
        "key": "q"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_r",
        "key": "w"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_gun_start",
        "key": "enter"
      },
      {
        "setting": "input_player1_gun_select",
        "key": "rshift"
      }
    ],
    "hotkeys": [
